WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.960
Early in the history of our solar system,

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.270
something mysteriously knocked Earth

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.410
slightly off its axis.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.990
So today we tilt at 23.5 degrees.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.220
But what would happen
if we tilted even more?

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.090
What if Earth spun sideways on its axis?

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.930
Well, it wouldn't take long
before utter chaos ensued.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.330
One of the most important consequences

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.690
of Earth's axial tilt is the seasons.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.980
Seasons happen because the tilt points

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.480
different parts of the
planet toward the sun

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.760
at different times of the year.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.970
But the tilt also means that
different parts of the globe

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:44.190
receive different amounts of
sunlight during each season.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.240
And that's where a more extreme tilt

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.640
starts to cause problems.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.250
Right now, during the summer
in the Northern Hemisphere,

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:56.150
places far north, like Utqiagvik, Alaska,

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.016
receive 24 hours of sunlight

00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:01.550
for 82 days straight.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.890
Because Earth is tilted
far enough on its axis

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.780
that as the planet rotates,

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.020
Utqiagvik never leaves direct sunlight.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.620
On the other hand, the contiguous US

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:16.950
receives a max of 17 hours
a day, because after that

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.790
it rotates out of daytime
sunlight and into night.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:25.790
But if we tilted Earth's axis
even more, to 90 degrees,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.620
the US would get sunlight
24/7, around the clock,

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.550
for months on end.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.910
And it's not just the US;

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.500
the entire Northern
Hemisphere would be like this.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.180
At first, animals would take
advantage of the extra light

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.230
to find and eat more food,
just like Alaskan birds,

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.370
which feed their chicks extra
nutrition in the summer,

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.620
resulting in faster-growing babies

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.750
than their southern counterparts.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.930
And plant growth would explode,

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:59.370
since they get their energy
directly from sunlight.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:02.120
Farms in northern Alaska, for example,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.300
grow cabbages the size of
rottweilers in the summer.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:11.010
But while animals and plants
would thrive, humans wouldn't.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:14.700
We evolved to be active during
the day and sleep at night.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.020
But if we were exposed
to unending sunlight,

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:21.500
our brains would stop producing
the hormone melatonin,

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.640
which we need to sleep at night.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.040
And that could lead to sleep deprivation,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.120
depression, and, ultimately,
a more severe, chronic version

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.570
of these symptoms called
seasonal affective disorder,

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.130
which already affects 9% of Alaskans,

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:41.410
compared to just 6% of
the entire United States.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:45.370
But that's less of a
worry than the floods.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:48.900
Temperatures at the North
Pole would more than double,

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:53.670
to 38 degrees Celsius
from 15.5 degrees Celsius.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.530
That's hotter than temperatures
at the equator today.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.950
As a result, Greenland's
ice cap would melt,

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.150
causing sea levels to rise by 7 meters,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.800
and flood nearly every
coastal city on Earth.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.760
Say goodbye to New York,
Copenhagen, and Tokyo.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.840
To make matters worse, the warmer seas

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.380
would trigger stronger and
more frequent hurricanes,

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:22.330
which form when sea water
evaporates at the surface.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.940
And the weather wouldn't get better

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.760
when winter comes six months later.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.010
Out of reach of the sun's direct beams

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.780
for months at a time, the
hemisphere would get colder

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:35.080
than any winter on record.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.520
Swirls of frigid air,
called a polar vortex,

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.900
which are normally dissipated
by warm air in the tropics,

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.220
could travel all the
way down to the equator.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:49.670
Imagine blizzards in
Florida, Brazil, Kenya!

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.220
And all those thriving plants,

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.910
they'd die from a lack of sunlight.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:58.090
Agriculture would collapse
as ecosystems crumble

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.400
and mass extinctions pile up.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.845
And there would be even
more floods, because

00:04:03.845 --> 00:04:07.626
meanwhile, the Southern
Hemisphere is getting toasty

00:04:07.626 --> 00:04:12.120
and the South Pole is home
to 90% of the world's ice.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.490
The constant sunlight
would raise its temperature

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:19.230
to 38 degrees Celsius
from -28 degrees Celsius,

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.610
melting the ice and raising sea levels

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.890
by a whopping 61 meters.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.680
That's almost as tall as
the Leaning Tower of Pisa.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.410
Greenland's flood would look
like a puddle in comparison.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.030
So all in all, while a few extra hours

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.490
in the summer sun would be nice,

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:40.240
let's leave the extra seasons to Alaska

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.480
and be glad the Earth is
tilted exactly as it is.

